SUMMARY:BugFest 2026
DESCRIPTION:Exhibits & Activities | Presentations & Performances | Café Insecta | Accessibility | Getting Here & Parking \nHappy 30th BugFest\nThree decades of creepy\, crawly and fluttering fun come together for the Museum’s biggest celebration yet. This year’s theme\, “Hoppers\,” spotlights treehoppers\, planthoppers and leafhoppers. \nExplore more than 100 exhibits\, crafts\, games and activities celebrating the world of arthropods. Ask entomologists and other scientists about all things bugs. Satisfy your curiosity and appetite with buggy culinary creations at Café Insecta. Enjoy science talks and live performances throughout the day. \nFREE and for all ages. \n\nMember Perks\nMuseum Members get VIP status at BugFest. The first 500 Members to arrive will receive a Member VIP pass to unlock special benefits. Don’t bug out if you arrive late! Members can access their VIP perks with their membership card. VIP passes can be picked up at the Member tent. \nSkip the line at Café Insecta with the Member Fast Lane and enjoy tasty bug-filled treats prepared by local chefs. Plus\, Members always receive unlimited FREE admission to special exhibitions\, invitations to exclusive events\, and save 20% in our gift shops and 10% in cafés! \nJoin or renew now\, get a free BugFest T-shirt!\n \nPurchase or renew your membership at BugFest or online September 1–19 with code “Hop26” and receive a free BugFest t-shirt on the day of the event! Not a Member? Join Today! \n\nVolunteer\n\nWant to be part of BugFest? Volunteer with us! Jobs span logistical tasks (setup\, breakdown\, meal service\, t-shirt sales\, etc.)\, educational stations\, and kids’ crafts and activities. It’s loads of fun and you get a free BugFest t-shirt. Volunteers who work 2+ shifts get free lunch. \nVolunteers must be 13 years old to volunteer without a parent. Volunteers must be 10 years old to volunteer with a parent. \nRegistration is live! Create a Get Connected account or login to register. Questions? Contact Kari Wouk. \n\nExhibitors\n\nApplications for vending and exhibiting are closed for this year. If you would like to be added to the list for next year\, please fill out the interest form! Apply Here. \n\n 
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/bugfest-2026/
LOCATION:Downtown Raleigh\, 11 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Accessible,Adults,All Ages,Children,Educators,K-12 Students,Special Events,Teens
ORGANIZER;CN="Miranda%20Dowdy":MAILTO:miranda.dowdy@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.7822735;-78.6395502
